WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.120
Local model serving is not automatically safe just because it runs nearby.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.785
Operators should understand what address the service listens on, who can reach it,

00:00:07.785 --> 00:00:09.750
and which applications are expected to use it.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.760
A service intended for one user on a local machine has different risk than a service

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.865
reachable by a team,

00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:17.000
a lab network, or other internal systems.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.990
Network exposure should be a deliberate architecture decision.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.720
If a model service is reachable by other hosts, teams may need authentication,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.500
authorization, firewalling, reverse proxy controls, monitoring, and documented ownership.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.000
The exact controls depend on the environment, but the principle is consistent:

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.500
do not assume that being internal means access is automatically appropriate.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.995
Data handling is also part of security operations.

00:00:37.995 --> 00:00:43.000
Prompts, retrieved context, file contents, and outputs may contain secrets, credentials,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.920
personal data, internal plans, customer information, or confidential work product.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.545
Integrations should avoid logging sensitive prompts or outputs unless a governed process

00:00:51.545 --> 00:00:52.990
explicitly requires it.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.970
When logs are necessary, teams should consider redaction, retention,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.250
and who can read them.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.140
Defensive operation focuses on clear access boundaries, privacy-aware logging,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.500
and supportable ownership.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.060
Operators should know which workflows are approved,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.540
which users or applications can reach the service, what data classes are allowed,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.990
and who reviews changes.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:15.000
These choices keep local AI useful without turning it into an unmanaged internal endpoint.
